## Part 6: Top/Bottom PCB Strategy (Dual Variants)

### 6.1 Why Dual-Sided

For dual-C5 and dual-E22 variants, two radio modules + supporting components cannot reasonably fit on a single side of a ~32–35 × 28 mm board while maintaining antenna clearance. Top/bottom placement is standard practice in compact RF designs.

### 6.2 Placement Strategy

| Component | Side | Position | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| U1 (Primary radio) | Top | Near one short edge, antenna toward edge | 15 mm keep-out from antenna |
| U1B (Secondary radio) | Bottom | Near **opposite** corner, **rotated 90°** | Orthogonal orientation for polarization diversity |
| U2 (USB bridge) | Top (or bottom) | Near USB-C edge | Short USB traces |
| U6 (SD mux) | Same side as U2 or between modules | Central | Minimize SDIO trace length |
| U3, U4, U5 (power) | Top or bottom | Grouped together | Wide power traces |
| J1 (USB-C) | Edge-mount | Centered on short edge | — |
| J2 / XU7 (storage) | Top | Near U6 | Short SDIO traces |
| Battery | — | In remaining space | Long/thin format; may span full length |

### 6.3 Stack-up Recommendation

| Layer | Purpose |
|---|---|
| L1 (Top) | U1, U2, U6, passives, short RF traces |
| L2 | **Solid ground plane** (critical for RF isolation) |
| L3 | Power (3V3, VBAT, VBUS) + non-critical routing |
| L4 (Bottom) | U1B, remaining passives |

4-layer is **strongly recommended** for dual variants. Single C5 variants can use 2-layer but 4-layer is preferred for all.

### 6.4 RF Isolation Measures

- **15 mm minimum keep-out** around each module's PCB antenna (all layers: no copper, no components, no traces)
- Antenna faces board edge
- **Via fence/stitching** around each RF zone
- Orthogonal module orientation (90° rotation between U1 and U1B)
- Firmware band steering (one radio on 5 GHz, other on 2.4 GHz if needed)

### 6.5 Thermal Notes

- Dual radios + bridge generate noticeable heat in sealed Charm
- Spread modules to opposite corners/sides
- Thermal vias under hot components to inner copper planes
- Firmware throttling if temperature exceeds safe threshold
- Larger battery acts as partial heat sink
- **Mandatory:** Thermal soak test on prototype (charging + sustained transfer at high ambient)

